{
  "chapter": "durability/agent-as-workflow",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "One rule decides the layout: a model call cannot be replayed, so it is an activity, and",
    "every other placement decision follows from that one.",
    "The deadline cannot read the clock inside workflow code. It becomes a run timeout the",
    "server enforces even when the worker is wedged.",
    "Everything an activity returns is written to the event history and journalled forever, so",
    "truncate and project inside the activity rather than after it.",
    "A model activity must heartbeat, or a slow call is declared timed out and retried while",
    "it is still running, and you pay for both.",
    "Idempotency keys become trivially correct here, because the workflow id is stable by",
    "construction rather than by discipline.",
    "Of the bounds from Part II, the deadline moves to the platform and the step and cost caps",
    "remain entirely yours."
  ],
  "config": {
    "maxPayloadBytes": 2000000,
    "maxHistoryBytes": 4000000,
    "activityTimeoutMs": 30000
  },
